{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>the men of Gibeon</b> — Missing a vav. The correct reading is either ואנשי גבעון (\"and the men of Gibeon\"), or מלטיה וידון אנשי גבעון והמצפה (\"Melatiah and Jadon, the men of Gibeon and Mizpah\")." "<b>the throne of the governor of Beyond the River</b> — It is possible that לכסא is a person's name, the lamed indicating the substantive, and the meaning: they undertook to build for the person who is the throne-designate, i.e., the governor of Beyond the River; similar to פחת מואב. Or לכסא is a place name nearby, and the phrase פחת עבר is a person's name, and the meaning: those mentioned joined hands to build as far as Likhsa, the governor of Beyond the River. This is the correct reading."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:59.728000883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}